&= 2s^2 - 2s^2 \cos (240^\circ + \theta).
\end{align*}By the Law of Cosines on triangle $ACE_3,$
\[CE_3^2 = 2s^2 - 2s^2 \cos \theta.\]By the Law of Cosines on triangle $ACE_4,$
\[CE_2^2 = 2s^2 - 2s^2 \cos (120^\circ + \theta).\]Note that
\begin{align*}
